How do drones return to home automatically ?
→ Drones use GPS to record the take-off location.
→ If the battery is low or the signal is lost, the Return-to-Home (RTH) feature starts automatically.
→ The drone files back to the saved location.
→ It lands safely without the pilot’s control.
Explain obstacle avoidance in drones ?
→ Obstacle avoidance helps the drone detect and avoid obstacles.
→ It uses sensors like LiDAR, Ultrasonic, Cameras, and Optical Flow.
→ When an obstacle is detected, the drone slows down, stops, or changes its direction.
→ This prevents accidents and makes flying safer.
